=============================================================== Neal add this method on Monday, September 22, 2003 11:14:23 AM. =============================================================== Registered Date: 2003.09.21 Reported Date: 2003.09.21 Fixed Date: - Version: 1.2.2003.0829 Environment: Windows XP + VS.NET 2002J Symptoms This problem occurs on Edit, Mask, Date, and Number controls.
Invoking Focus method in KeyExit event will make caret on the focused control disappeared.
This phenomenone won't occur when the TabIndex of focused control is next to the Focus invoking control.
Steps On a new Form of new project, place one Edit control and two textBox controls. Set TabIndex properties as follows. edit1.TabIndex = 0; textBox1.TabIndex = 1; textBox2.TabIndex = 2;
Write the following code in the Edit's KeyExit event procedure. textBox2.Focus(); Run the project and press Tab key on edit1 control. String on textBox2 is highlighted but caret won't appear. Press any keys, then they will be input on textBox2. If you change the code to as follows. Then caret will appear properly. textBox1.Focus();

